# Line endings are NOT converted, in either direction.
#
# This is not a style choice. MANIFEST.sha256 records the SHA-256 of every file
# as deposited, and the guarantee it makes is that a clone is bit-for-bit what
# was published. Any end-of-line conversion on commit or checkout would break
# that guarantee on some platform.
#
# The parent repository runs with core.autocrlf=true and no .gitattributes, so
# its Windows working tree holds a mix: 30 of these text files are CRLF on disk
# and 71 are LF. The copies here preserve each file exactly as it was, which is
# what makes the byte-identity claim in PROVENANCE.md section 1.2 true. The
# mixed endings are therefore a property of the source, faithfully carried over,
# not an oversight.
#
# `-text` disables all conversion. Verify after cloning with:
#     sha256sum -c MANIFEST.sha256
* -text
